{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cv9a2WQBEovJtjsh1GogZz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the relevant information in the KIP-1271 discussion document.\\\\n\\\\n**Answer:** Kafka Streams state stores do **NOT** preserve record headers with a 2-byte length field encoding. Instead, according to the KIP-1271 design decisions:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Initial Decision (Window 8 - Jan 14, 2026)**: A two-byte header size field was explicitly **removed** as redundant, since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Updated Decision (Window 17 - Jan 29, 2026)**: When the header size field was reintroduced to enable lazy deserialization, it was implemented as a **varint** encoding rather than a fixed 2-byte format. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead while achieving efficient skipping.\\\\n\\\\n**Cited from:**\\\\n- `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67-68 and 111)\\\\n\\\\nThe key quote: \\\\\\\"A varint `header_size` field is now introduced to enable lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"prs/21297-kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":20.24,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":62928,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":9266,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0317348,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1372}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f551b707-af38-4008-b0ce-617b6bfac62a","uuid":"803343fe-8fbc-492e-830c-5d9dbf77eef3","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:51:05.944Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the relevant information in the KIP-1271 discussion document.\\\\n\\\\n**Answer:** Kafka Streams state stores do **NOT** preserve record headers with a 2-byte length field encoding. Instead, according to the KIP-1271 design decisions:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Initial Decision (Window 8 - Jan 14, 2026)**: A two-byte header size field was explicitly **removed** as redundant, since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Updated Decision (Window 17 - Jan 29, 2026)**: When the header size field was reintroduced to enable lazy deserialization, it was implemented as a **varint** encoding rather than a fixed 2-byte format. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead while achieving efficient skipping.\\\\n\\\\n**Cited from:**\\\\n- `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67-68 and 111)\\\\n\\\\nThe key quote: \\\\\\\"A varint `header_size` field is now introduced to enable lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"prs/21297-kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":20.24,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":62928,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":9266,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0317348,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1372}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the relevant information in the KIP-1271 discussion document.\\n\\n**Answer:** Kafka Streams state stores do **NOT** preserve record headers with a 2-byte length field encoding. Instead, according to the KIP-1271 design decisions:\\n\\n1. **Initial Decision (Window 8 - Jan 14, 2026)**: A two-byte header size field was explicitly **removed** as redundant, since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes.\\n\\n2. **Updated Decision (Window 17 - Jan 29, 2026)**: When the header size field was reintroduced to enable lazy deserialization, it was implemented as a **varint** encoding rather than a fixed 2-byte format. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead while achieving efficient skipping.\\n\\n**Cited from:**\\n- `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67-68 and 111)\\n\\nThe key quote: \\\"A varint `header_size` field is now introduced to enable lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges. This matches Kafka's serialization standards and avoids fixed-size field overhead.\\\"\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\",\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\",\"prs/21297-kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\"],\"seconds\":20.24,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":62928,\"cache_write_tokens\":9266,\"cost_usd\":0.0317348,\"input_tokens\":50,\"output_tokens\":1372}}"}}}
